# .dockerignore
#
# Fallback for a build with the repo root as context whose Dockerfile has no
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore beside it. Every service in the compose files has
# one, and BuildKit reads that in place of this file, so a change here does not
# reach those builds: make it in each Dockerfile.dockerignore as well.
#
# Patterns are relative to the repo root. A bare pattern such as `.env` would
# match only at the root, so each one carries a `**/` prefix to match at any
# depth.

# Python caches: regenerated automatically, and must not land in an image.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Environment files: must never be baked into an image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Virtual environments and Node dependencies: installed fresh inside the image.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/env
**/node_modules

# Test artefacts.
**/htmlcov
**/.coverage
**/coverage.xml

# Editor and OS noise.
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/.vscode
**/.idea

# Git internals.
.git
**/.gitignore
